.TH CRASH 1
.SH NAME
crash \- a service that fails or hangs (a test)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crash
.br
.B crash hang
.I port
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments,
.B crash
ends at once with status 3: it tests that
.BR init (8)
backs off and gives up on a service that cannot start
.RB ( "svc add crasher /bin/crash" ).
.PP
.B crash hang
.I port
is a stuck server: it creates
.I port
and never answers, so that init's watcher must end it
.RB ( "svc add \-w" " " \fIport\fR " ...).
.SH EXIT STATUS
3; 4 if
.I port
cannot be created.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR svc (8),
.BR init (8)
